    {
      "title": "White-collar hiring rises 14% in August, led by auto, healthcare: Report",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/industry/news/white-collar-hiring-rises-14-in-august-led-by-auto-healthcare-report-126090800441_1.html",
      "description": "India's white-collar hiring registered a 14 per cent year-on-year growth in August, driven by sectors including auto, healthcare and retail, a report said on Tuesday.\nThe overall Naukri JobSpeak Index touched 3,028 compared to 2,664 in August last year, according to a report by Naukri.com, Info Edge's flagship brand.\nAugust saw hiring growth across both IT and non-IT sectors and across experience levels. However, the hiring growth needs to be viewed in the context of the festive calendar, with a larger part of the festive period falling in August last year and shifting to September this year.\n\"We will have a clearer view of the underlying hiring trend as we move through the festive quarter,\" Info Edge (India) Ltd MD and CEO Hitesh Oberoi said.\nThe Naukri JobSpeak report is a monthly index that tracks trends in India's job market and hiring activity, based on new job postings (including free job listings) and recruiter searches on Naukri.com's platform.\nThe report further revealed",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-09-08T07:13:39"
